      en: "Simulambuco Treaty Monument is a remarkable feature of the geography and culture of Angola. A monument commemorating the 1885 Treaty of Simulambuco, which established Cabinda as a Portuguese protectorate. The treaty was signed by Portuguese and local rulers. Basis for Cabinda's separate status. Important symbol of regional history. This site holds particular significance in the history of Angola. Like many notable places in Angola, it combines regional character with wider significance. Thus, this place contributes to the diverse profile of Angola."
