      en: "Fort of São Pedro da Barra is a remarkable feature of the geography and culture of Angola. A 17th-century defensive structure in Luanda, built by the Portuguese after recapturing the city from the Dutch. Built around 1703 on ruins of an older fort. Later served as a quarantine station. Candidate for World Heritage status. This site holds particular significance in the history of Angola. Like many notable places in Angola, it combines regional character with wider significance. Thus, this place contributes to the diverse profile of Angola."
